                "text": "Analyse the training examples:\n\nIn Example 1:\n- Input has size 8x10.\n- There is a central rectangle of color 2 (with two intruder pixels of color 7).\n- The bounding box of color 2 (and 7) is rows 1 to 6 (height 6) and cols 3 to 7 (width 5).\n- Output is 6x5.\n- The intruder pixels in this rectangle:\n  - (row 3, col 4): in local coords, row = 3 - 1 = 2, col = 4 - 3 = 1.\n  - (row 5, col 6): local row = 5 - 1 = 4, col = 6 - 3 = 3.\n- Output grid:\n  - Output has 7 in col 1 and row 2?\n    - Row 2 of output: all 7s!\n    - Col 1 of output: all 7s!\n  - Also:\n    - Row 4 of output: all 7s!\n    - Col 3 of output: all 7s!\n  - Everywhere else is 2.\n  - So for each intruder pixel at (r, c) within the inner rectangle:\n    - Entire row r and entire column c become the intruder color (7)!\n    - At intersections, it is 7.\n    - Base color is 2.\n\nLet's check Example 2:\n- Inner rectangle:\n  - Base color is 5.\n  - Bounding box: rows 2 to 7 (height 6), cols 3 to 8 (width 6).\n  - Intruder: color 3 at (row 3, col 5).\n  - Local coords: row 3 - 2 = 1, col 5 - 3 = 2.\n  - Output is 6x6.\n  - In output:\n    - Row 1 is all 3s.\n    - Col 2 is all 3s.\n    - Everywhere else is 5.\n  - Exactly matches!\n\nLet's check Example 3:\n- Inner rectangle:\n  - Base color is 6.\n  - Bounding box: rows 4 to 9 (height 6), cols 4 to 9 (width 6).\n  - Intruder: color 4 at (row 5, col 6).\n  - Local coords: row 5 - 4 = 1, col 6 - 4 = 2.\n  - Output:\n    - Row 1 is all 4s.\n    - Col 2 is all 4s.\n    - Everywhere else is 6.\n  - Exactly matches!\n\nTransformation rule:\n1. Identify the prominent rectangular block (which is surrounded by diverse noise/random numbers, or simply a monochromatic rectangle with a few \"intruder/target\" pixels).\n2. The rectangle has a dominant background color $B$, and one or more intruder pixels of color $C$ (or potentially different colors, but here same color).\n3. Extract the rectangle of dimensions $H \\times W$.\n4. In the